          "quality_risk": false,
          "reason": "requests queue at max_concurrent_requests 8 with 120 waiting, and the doubling rule offers only 16; sized in tokens (about 2064 per request), 29 requests fill 85% of the 71056-token pool a cold start gives (a new cap restarts the engine cold), so 29 is worth trying. It usually cuts queueing (TTFT) but slows each token (TPOT) - measure both",
          "test": "about 11 min on this setup (this run: 294 s to load, 6.1 min to warm up and measure)",
